  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836972",
      "title": "Sending Data with POST Requests",
      "sourceHash": "d0338be83f237a882bbefa26df5aade2828a5d3774f534a70b0a937b96471f95",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.91,
          "en": "Now, fetching those available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.91,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "here is the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 8.25,
          "en": "Of course, I now also wanna make sure that we can click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.25,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "on those places and add them to our selection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "And as we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "I also wanna send a request to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "so that our selection is stored there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 21.51,
          "en": "Because at the moment, if I reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.51,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "my selection is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.05,
          "en": "So of course, then thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.05,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "I also wanna fetch my storage selection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 28.593,
          "en": "from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.52,
          "end": 30.84,
          "en": "And therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 30.84,
          "end": 35.84,
          "en": "this dummy backend indeed does have two routes to endpoints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "that allow us to store the places we picked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 42.213,
          "en": "and to get our places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 45.9,
          "en": "As mentioned earlier, here in this dummy app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.9,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "the places would theoretically be shared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "across all users that use this web app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "so they would all be managing the same selection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 55.38,
          "en": "But for this demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "this is absolutely fine and no problem, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "So let's now start by making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "that when we select a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 66.63,
          "en": "we actually send that updated selection of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.63,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 71.31,
          "en": "Now for this, we should go to the App.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "because it's here where I'm outputting the userPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 80.03999999999999,
          "en": "and it's here where I have my userPlaces state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "which is this array of places that is updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "whenever I select a place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 89.19,
          "en": "And it's therefore now here, inside of handleSelectPlace,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 92.00999999999999,
          "en": "where I don't just wanna update this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.00999999999999,
          "end": 97.00999999999999,
          "en": "but where I also wanna send my updated array of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.013,
          "en": "to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "To do that, we need to add some code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 103.28999999999999,
          "en": "after we updated the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.28999999999999,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "Or also here, before we update the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "and I'll get back to which position you might wanna choose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 111.813,
          "en": "for which reasons soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 116.58,
          "en": "So I'll start here by sending my request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.58,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "after updating the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "And to do that, we can again use the fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 124.32,
          "en": "because as I mentioned earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 127.29,
          "en": "this function can also be used to send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.29,
          "end": 131.85,
          "en": "that want to change data, not just to get data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.85,
          "end": 134.19,
          "en": "even though the name might imply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 137.043,
          "en": "that you can only fetch data, but that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "Now I will actually not write my fetching code here, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 146.9,
          "en": "or my sending code, but instead, I'll use that http.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.45,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "and add a new function to this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 154.29,
          "en": "A new exported async function that should be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.29,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "for updating the user places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 159.25,
          "en": "Therefore I'll name it, updateUserPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 162.603,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 168.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now here, I expect to get an array of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.32999999999998,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "that should be sent to the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "because this dummy backend API here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "this dummy backend server, expects to get an array of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 180.963,
          "en": "that will then simply be stored in a file there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "And therefore here, I must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 186.003,
          "en": "that I send such an array of places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "As mentioned, this can be done with the fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "And here, we, again, need to specify the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 196.023,
          "en": "to which the request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.86,
          "end": 201.45,
          "en": "Here, to localhost:3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "and then user-places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 206.31,
          "en": "That's the path that should be targeted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.31,
          "end": 209.073,
          "en": "for this dummy backend I'm providing to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.72,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "But now, it's actually not enough anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 215.613,
          "en": "to just send the request like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 219.3,
          "en": "Instead, here, to change those places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.3,
          "end": 223.07999999999998,
          "en": "a put request is expected by the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.07999999999998,
          "end": 227.19,
          "en": "So, we must change the http method that's used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 229.23,
          "en": "Because the default is the get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.23,
          "end": 230.94299999999998,
          "en": "but that's the wrong method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 234.54,
          "en": "And you do this with help of a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.54,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "that can be passed to fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 239.28,
          "en": "which is a configuration object that allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.28,
          "end": 241.623,
          "en": "to configure the outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "Here we can, for example, set the method property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 249.78,
          "en": "and define which http request method should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.78,
          "end": 251.673,
          "en": "In this case, for example, PUT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.38,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "In addition, we also must add the body property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "to define which data should be attached as a request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 263.073,
          "en": "to that outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 266.7,
          "en": "And here, that should be my places array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.7,
          "end": 270.3,
          "en": "Though, that data must actually be in a format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 271.98,
          "en": "that is attachable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.98,
          "end": 276.75,
          "en": "and JavaScript arrays are not an attachable format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.75,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "Instead, this should be converted into this JSON format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 281.913,
          "en": "which I mentioned before first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.93,
          "end": 286.473,
          "en": "So here, we should call JSON stringify places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.85,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "This will convert this places array into JSON format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 293.283,
          "en": "and this can now be attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 298.35,
          "en": "Last but not least, some extra headers should be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.35,
          "end": 302.67,
          "en": "So, some extra metadata that's attached to the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.67,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "And here, specifically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "you should add the Content-Type header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 311.79,
          "en": "and set this to application/json to inform the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.79,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "that the data attached to this request will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 317.16,
          "en": "in JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.16,
          "end": 319.62,
          "en": "This is required to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.62,
          "end": 323.58299999999997,
          "en": "that the data is extracted successfully on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 325.68,
          "end": 328.62,
          "en": "Well, with that, we can then await the result of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 328.62,
          "end": 330.543,
          "en": "and get back our response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.13,
          "end": 333.84000000000003,
          "en": "And then just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 337.713,
          "en": "we can take a look at that response, parse it, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 339.03,
          "end": 342.12,
          "en": "So here, I'll get my response data, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.12,
          "end": 347.073,
          "en": "by calling response.json and awaiting that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 348.93,
          "end": 352.62,
          "en": "And I also wanna check if response is not okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 352.62,
          "end": 355.2,
          "en": "So if we got an error status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 355.2,
          "end": 358.867,
          "en": "in which case I, again, wanna throw a new error where I say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 358.867,
          "end": 362.58,
          "en": "\"Failed to update user data.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 362.58,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "And then here at the end, I can return my response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 369.24,
          "en": "and then there, actually, the message property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.24,
          "end": 372.42,
          "en": "because if we take a look at this backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.42,
          "end": 375.39,
          "en": "and there, the put user-places route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 375.39,
          "end": 378.93,
          "en": "we see that the response will contain an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.93,
          "end": 380.64300000000003,
          "en": "with a message property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.31,
          "end": 384.75,
          "en": "Though here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.75,
          "end": 387.75,
          "en": "I will actually not use that data, but nonetheless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 387.75,
          "end": 389.253,
          "en": "we can return it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 390.93,
          "end": 395.25,
          "en": "So with that, we got our updateUserPlaces function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.25,
          "end": 397.26,
          "en": "and back in the app JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.26,
          "end": 401.76,
          "en": "we can now use this function after updating the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.76,
          "end": 404.913,
          "en": "inside of this handleSelectPlace function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 406.38,
          "end": 409.397,
          "en": "So here, we can then call updateUserPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 411.69,
          "end": 416.613,
          "en": "and import this function from the http.js file, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 419.61,
          "end": 422.67,
          "en": "And then down here, where I am calling it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 422.67,
          "end": 425.403,
          "en": "I wanna pass my updated places to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 426.24,
          "end": 427.8,
          "en": "Now you could think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 427.8,
          "end": 432.57,
          "en": "that we can therefore simply use our userPlaces state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 432.57,
          "end": 435,
          "en": "because I have just updated the state here",
